  "summary": "New preprints and a paper apply sequence-derived classification to metagenomic reads, M. tuberculosis spoligotyping, gonococcal susceptibility and Cas9…",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is extracting actionable microbial identity or phenotype from sequence data. MicrobeRT fine-tunes Nucleotide Transformer, DNABERT and HyenaDNA for metagenomic read taxonomy and resistance gene detection. HiSpoT provides a one-tube dual-barcode PCR workflow for NGS spoligotyping of Mycobacterium tuberculosis complex. SensiTyper applies rule-based prediction of gonococcal antimicrobial susceptibility from WGS, tested on 13,701 genomes, to guide individualized treatment. NanoPAMDA extends sequence mining to metagenome-derived Cas9 effectors for PAM characterization. What differs from the earlier framing is a shift from amplicon classifiers toward pretrained genomic language models alongside typing and clinical-prediction tools. The items differ in target, method and maturity, so this is a shared direction rather than a single algorithm.",
